<section class="hero">
  <div class="wrap hero__in">
    <div class="hero__text">
      <span class="eyebrow">International</span>
      <h1>For communities <span>that trade across borders</span></h1>
      <p class="lede">AmChams, bi-national chambers, World Trade Centers, export associations and companies entering the U.S. market: your members compete online in one market, with teams from different countries.</p>
      <div class="btns">
        <button type="button" class="btn" data-lead="">Request a demo game</button>
        <a class="btn btn--line" href="#programs">See programs</a>
      </div>
      <p class="undercta">Free 60-minute demo for your board or your team. Prices in U.S. dollars.</p>
    </div>
    {% include "partials/selector.njk" %}
  </div>
</section>

<div class="flow">
<section class="sect" id="who" aria-labelledby="whoTitle">
  <div class="wrap">
    <span class="eyebrow">Who it's for</span>
    <h2 id="whoTitle">Members whose market is bigger than one country</h2>
    <div class="cards cards--4">
      <article class="card">
        <span class="card__tag">AmChams</span>
        <h3>American chambers abroad</h3>
        <p>A program for international business communities, run online in English.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="card">
        <span class="card__tag">Bi-national</span>
        <h3>Bi-national chambers in the U.S.</h3>
        <p>Members from two economies meet in one market and see how each side competes.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="card">
        <span class="card__tag">Trade</span>
        <h3>World Trade Centers and export associations</h3>
        <p>For companies that import, export or sell abroad.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="card">
        <span class="card__tag">Market entry</span>
        <h3>Companies entering the U.S.</h3>
        <p>Rehearse the first year in a market where local players already compete.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="sect sect--tint" id="focus" aria-labelledby="focusTitle">
  <div class="wrap split">
    <div>
      <span class="eyebrow">What changes</span>
      <h2 id="focusTitle">Entering a market where locals already compete</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="prose">
      <p class="lede">Teams from different countries meet in one market, and each brings its own business habits. The game shows what happens when those habits collide.</p>
      <ul class="ticks">
        <li>Pricing against incumbents who know the customers</li>
        <li>The cash gap of long payment terms</li>
        <li>Advertising in a market you do not know yet</li>
        <li>When trade finance helps — and when a loan only moves the gap</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Sponsors for international programs are usually banks with trade finance.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="sect sect--dark" id="open-games" aria-labelledby="ogTitle">
  <div class="wrap">
    <span class="eyebrow">Open games</span>
    <h2 id="ogTitle">Try the game at an open session</h2>
    <p class="lede">Open online games in English run every week on U.S. and London time. Anyone can join — an easy way for your staff or board to try the game before a demo.</p>
    <div class="btns">
      <a class="btn" href="{{ site.game.url }}#calendar">See open games on marketgame.club</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

